{"id":218610,"login":"trask"},"findings":[{"body":"<!-- ccr-overview-v2 -->\n\n### \ud83d\udfe1 Changes recommended\n\nThe library README incorrectly claims JFR-sourced GC duration points include `jvm.gc.cause`.\n\n<details open>\n<summary><strong>1 open finding</strong></summary>\n\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/low-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/low-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/low-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Low severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Clarify JFR and JMX behavior for jvm.gc.duration](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation/pull/20376#discussion_r4233122049) \u00b7 New\n</details>\n\n\ud83e\udde0 **Review effort:** Balanced","comment_id":null,"key":"review:5473668551","kind":"body","line":null,"path":null,"review_id":5473668551},{"body":"[General] This is only true for JMX-sourced GC metrics. When `jvm.gc.duration` is selected for JFR, the JFR handlers record only `jvm.gc.name` and `jvm.gc.action` (for example, `G1GarbageCollectionHandler.java:30-31,53`), so this sentence misdocuments a supported selector path. Scope the claim to JMX and clarify the JFR behavior.","comment_commit_id":"68d09a93c8e89131117e55f2b79b87393824ee1c","comment_id":4233122049,"key":"inline:4233122049","kind":"inline","line":218,"original_commit_id":"68d09a93c8e89131117e55f2b79b87393824ee1c","original_line":218,"path":"instrumentation/runtime-telemetry/library/README.md","review_commit_id":"68d09a93c8e89131117e55f2b79b87393824ee1c","review_id":5473668551,"review_submitted_at":"2026-10-09T18:03:52Z","root_author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"thread_context":[{"author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","ty